{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536391-interesting-spots-for-a-game","id":1536391,"title":"Interesting spots for a game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-27T16:13:44-07:00","id":1536391,"title":"Interesting spots for a game?","content":"I have ideas for a game setting but right now it is feeling rather generic. I don't want to use New Orleans, LA, or Las Vegas but I haven't worked out any other city that gives me a good High Weirdness vibe. Feel free to throw out some ideas for locations that you think would make a great setting.<br /> <br /> If I get to run the game it will likely be online so while local to me would work it isn't critical.<br /> <br /> One thought I did have was Prague or Budapest but I am slightly hesitant about using a non-US city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T17:52:06-07:00","id":1536393,"title":"","content":"Prague is a great option. Its a tech hub, has many ancient landmarks and <a href=\"https://pragueeventery.com/good-to-know/prague-myths-and-legends/\" target=\"_blank\">lots of local legends</a>. Venice might be another one with a lot of potential for plot hooks, with sigils of the old guilds hiding occult knowledge, secret treasures hidden in the during the sacking of Constantinople, secrets hidden beneath the waters affecting the very foundations of the city and mysterious gondoliers taking passengers to sections of La Serenissima that still stand in the Realms Invisible.<br /> <br /> Alesund in Norway might be another one, with the northern lights above, the Art Nouveau architecture, with secrets hidden in Mt Aksla or the Brosundet canal hiding the secrets of the city before the fire of 1904.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-27-2024, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T04:49:48-07:00","id":1536416,"title":"","content":"Prague does seem good with Budapest being a fundamentally similar setting in a slightly less cliched larger city. Thinking on it some more I think that having the characters be expats (not natives of the city)